# Aspire Orchestration

## AppHost (`aspire/AppHost/Program.cs`)

Starts PostgreSQL (data volume) + API + Vite. Injects `ConnectionStrings:enterprisestarterdb` and sets web to `VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api`; the web client normalizes it to `/api/v1` and uses the proxy for same-origin cookie/CSRF requests.

## ServiceDefaults

`aspire/ServiceDefaults/Extensions.cs` — OpenTelemetry (OTLP when `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` is set), health checks, service discovery, HTTP resilience.

API calls `builder.AddServiceDefaults()` and `app.MapDefaultEndpoints()`.

## Run

```bash
dotnet run --project aspire/AppHost
```

Use the **proxied web** URL from the dashboard for login.

## Docker vs Aspire

| | Aspire AppHost | Docker Compose |
|--|----------------|----------------|
| Purpose | Local dev | Optional deployment |
| Database | Aspire Postgres | Compose `postgres` |
| Migrations | API startup (dev) | One-shot `migrator` |
| Web | Vite (HMR) | nginx + static `dist` |
| Run | `dotnet run --project aspire/AppHost` | `docker compose up --build` |

Do not deploy AppHost. Do not replace Aspire with Docker for day-to-day development. Skill: `run-docker-deploy`.

